# The CPU_ONLY=1 compile gate, Windows 11 + RTX 3060, 2026-11-28
#
# Why it exists: the CPU path called DeviceMemoryFreeBytes(), whose declaration sits
# inside Kernel.cuh's OFXPLUGIN_WITH_CUDA block. Every local run built the CUDA path,
# where the declaration exists, so nothing local could see the break; windows.yml's
# CPU step hit it as error C3861 and would have stopped the first CI run there.
#
# The gate is now the step "== compile check: minimal-cuda-ofx with CPU_ONLY=1 ==" in
# ./run-tests.sh, on both routes: it configures and builds in
# templates/minimal-cuda-ofx/build-cpu-only (OFXPLUGIN_BUILD_DIR, so the CPU_ONLY
# configure cannot flip the cache of the CUDA build beside it), runs the artifact
# check without --cuda, and runs the contract suite on the fallback path.

## The step inside a full ./run-tests.sh pass (exit 0)

